# /sdd-next

Description:
  Advance to the next decision step or case.
  Checks completion status of current decision and linked tasks
  before determining the next action.

Usage:
  /sdd-next
  /sdd-next --decision DEC-<ID>
  /sdd-next --case CASE-<ID>
  /sdd-next --force

Options:
  --decision    Advance specific decision
  --case        Jump to specific case
  --force       Force advance even if incomplete (requires approval)

Behavior:
  1. Read current decision state from projects/{project_name}/decisions/
  2. Read linked tasks from projects/{project_name}/tasks/
  3. Check if current decision and ALL linked tasks are complete
  4. IF complete:
       - Move to next decision in the chain
       - If no more decisions, move to next case
       - If no more cases, signal workflow complete
  5. IF incomplete:
       - Identify which section is incomplete (decision or task)
       - Resume from that section
       - Do NOT advance to next case
  6. Record transition in decision history
  7. Update project state

CompletionCheck:
  decision_complete:
    - status = approved
    - all acceptance criteria met
    - implementation tasks linked

  task_complete:
    - status = DONE
    - all acceptance criteria met
    - tests pass
    - review passed

Output:
  [decision: DEC-XXX]
  [tasks_complete: true|false]
  [incomplete_section: decision|task|none]
  [action: advance|resume|complete]
  [next: <decision|case|workflow_complete>]

State: +
